WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.527
A submarine floods itself to dive.

00:00:02.537 --> 00:00:03.697
On purpose.

00:00:03.707 --> 00:00:05.365
Peel off the outer hull.

00:00:05.375 --> 00:00:07.853
On many subs, ballast tanks sit between

00:00:07.863 --> 00:00:08.805
the hulls.

00:00:08.815 --> 00:00:11.364
Open vents on top and valves below.

00:00:11.376 --> 00:00:13.742
Sea rushes in, air escapes.

00:00:13.752 --> 00:00:15.622
Less buoyant now, it sinks.

00:00:15.632 --> 00:00:17.728
Smaller tanks fine-tune depth.

00:00:17.738 --> 00:00:20.074
Diving planes angle its nose up or

00:00:20.084 --> 00:00:21.775
down as it moves.

00:00:21.785 --> 00:00:23.250
So how does it rise?

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.725
Shut the vents, blow in compressed air,

00:00:25.735 --> 00:00:27.535
and out goes the water.
